{
  "id": "03-best-time-to-buy-and-sell-stock",
  "title": "Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock",
  "track": "Arrays",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "topics": [
    "arrays"
  ],
  "source": "canonical Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "The input is an array of prices where prices[i] is the price on day i. Choose one day to buy and one strictly later day to sell. Return the largest profit (sell price minus buy price) achievable this way, or 0 when no choice turns a profit.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= len(prices) <= 5000",
    "0 <= prices[i] <= 10000"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    "prices"
  ],
  "functionName": "max_profit",
  "starterCode": "def max_profit(prices):\n    # Return the best profit from one buy followed by one later sell.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "prices": [
          6,
          2,
          8,
          1,
          5,
          9,
          3
        ]
      },
      "output": 8,
      "explanation": "Buy at 1 on day 3 and sell at 9 on day 5 for a profit of 8."
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "prices": [
          8,
          6,
          5,
          3,
          1
        ]
      },
      "output": 0,
      "explanation": "Prices only fall, so every trade loses money and the answer is 0."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "The best sell for a given buy day only depends on the highest price after it.",
    "Track a running value as you scan: the cheapest price seen so far. What single number do you compare against it at each step?",
    "Sweep left to right keeping min_so_far. At each day compute prices[i] - min_so_far and remember the best; update min_so_far before moving on."
  ],
  "solution": "Sweep the array once while tracking the lowest price seen so far. At each day the best profit selling that day is the day price minus that minimum, so the answer is the largest such difference. One pass: O(n) time, O(1) space.",
  "solutionCode": "def max_profit(prices):\n    best = 0\n    lowest = prices[0]\n    for price in prices:\n        if price < lowest:\n            lowest = price\n        elif price - lowest > best:\n            best = price - lowest\n    return best\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def max_profit(prices):\n    best = 0\n    for i in range(len(prices)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(prices)):\n            profit = prices[j] - prices[i]\n            if profit > best:\n                best = profit\n    return best\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include strictly falling prices, repeated prices, and the best pair near the end",
  "expectedComplexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
